# Interceptor: per-machine preferences (browser-only mode)
#
# Copy this file to:
#   ~/.myos/MYOS/USER/CUSTOMIZATIONS/SKILLS/Interceptor/preferences.env
# and fill in the values for YOUR machine, then edit that copy: never this
# example. Every Interceptor script sources it if present (LaunchTestProfile.sh,
# PreflightIsolation.sh, Capture.sh, EnsureTestProfile.sh). Nothing here has a
# safe cross-machine default: an absent/incomplete file means browser commands
# hard-fail with a remediation message rather than guessing and routing a tab
# into your real working/monitoring Chrome window. See SKILL.md and
# References/CommandReference.md for the full isolation contract.
#
# Derived directly from what ships under Tools/*.sh (grep -n 'INTERCEPTOR_\|CHROME_'
# skills/Interceptor/Tools/*.sh, 2026-07-28): nothing below is invented.

# ── Required: no safe default; PreflightIsolation.sh hard-fails without these ─

# The pinned Interceptor test context: the one browser tab/window Interceptor
# is ever allowed to drive. Freshly paired, this is a raw UUID assigned by the
# extension (e.g. "a1b2c3d4-..."). Durable fix: set a friendly name
# ("interceptor-test") once in the extension popup: friendly names survive
# extension reloads, raw UUIDs rot on every reload.
INTERCEPTOR_TEST_CONTEXT_ID=

# The on-disk Chrome profile DIRECTORY NAME for your dedicated test profile
# (not its display name): e.g. "Profile 4". Create this profile once via
# Chrome's avatar menu, sign it into whatever accounts Interceptor needs to
# test against, then map directory -> friendly name via:
#   ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Local State  (profile.info_cache)
# Deliberately NO default: defaulting to any concrete profile name risks
# opening your real working/monitoring profile by accident.
INTERCEPTOR_TEST_CHROME_PROFILE=

# ── Optional: safe defaults shown, commented out ──────────────────────────

# Browser app name LaunchTestProfile.sh passes to `open -a` on macOS.
# INTERCEPTOR_TEST_BROWSER=Google Chrome

# Linux only: the Chrome/Chromium binary LaunchTestProfile.sh execs directly
# (macOS uses `open -a "$INTERCEPTOR_TEST_BROWSER"` instead, above).
# CHROME_BIN=google-chrome

# Comma-separated context IDs PreflightIsolation.sh must treat as denied
# working/monitoring profiles, even if one is pinned by mistake. "Default" is
# always denied regardless of this list: set this only for OTHER named
# profiles you use for real work that Interceptor must never touch.
# INTERCEPTOR_WORKING_PROFILE_IDS=

# Where Pin.sh / PreflightIsolation.sh look for the upstream Interceptor
# extension source when re-pinning or freshness-checking the bundled
# Extension/ copy. Only relevant if you build the extension from source
# instead of installing the .pkg: see Workflows/Update.md.
# INTERCEPTOR_SRC=$HOME/Code/Interceptor

# Minimum standard-deviation Capture.sh accepts as "not a blank/degenerate
# frame" (the black-frame failure: page unhydrated or mid entrance-animation
# reads as a capture but isn't one). Raise this if a genuinely-loaded
# dark/low-contrast page keeps tripping the rejection; lower it only if you
# understand you are weakening that guard.
# INTERCEPTOR_MIN_STDDEV=0.017

# ── Not found in the shipped Tools/*.sh as of this writing ─────────────────
# If a future Interceptor release reads a variable not listed above, check:
#   skills/Interceptor/Tools/*.sh                    (grep -n 'INTERCEPTOR_\|CHROME_')
#   skills/Interceptor/SKILL.md
#   skills/Interceptor/References/CommandReference.md
# before inventing a name here. This file ships browser-only: the removed
# native/VM/iOS bridge variables (Swift bridge, TCC, Sparkle) are gone on
# purpose and are not TODOs.
